ccf(a,b){var s=A.cvR(A.afo(b,A.c4d(a)))
switch(a.a){case 0:return"I am really glad you told me. What you are carrying sounds very heavy, and I will not answer it with a lecture.\n\nPlease reach a real person right now. If you might act on these thoughts, or you have already hurt yourself, call your local emergency number now, move away from anything you could use to hurt yourself, and go to someone you trust.\n\n"+s+"\n\nIf you are worried about someone else, stay with them, and call the emergency number if they are in danger.\n\nAllah says: \u201cSay, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 39:53)\n\nYou are not a burden, and this pain does not get the last word. I am an app, not a person, so the people behind these lines matter more than anything I can say. I am still here."
case 1:return"I hear the weight behind that question, and I will answer it honestly, but first: if you are asking because you are in pain yourself, or because you lost someone this way, you are not being judged here.\n\nThe Qur\u2019an says: \u201cAnd do not kill yourselves [or one another]. Indeed, Allah is to you ever Merciful.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 4:29). That is never the first thing a hurting person needs to hear, and it is not the whole of what Islam says about you. Judgement of any person belongs to Allah alone. For a ruling about someone you lost, please ask a qualified scholar in person.\n\nAllah says: \u201cSay, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 39:53)\n\nIf any part of this is about you, please talk to a real person now:\n\n"+s+"\n\nIf you might act on these thoughts, call your local emergency number now."
case 2:return"I am sorry. What you describe is not okay, and it is not your fault. Nothing, not marriage, not family, not honour, makes it acceptable for someone to hurt, threaten or force you. Your safety comes first, and you do not have to decide anything tonight.\n\nIf you are in danger right now, call your local emergency number. If you can leave safely, go to someone you trust. These lines are for people in your situation:\n\n"+s+"\n\nIf you are asking for someone else, the same lines can advise you. A trusted imam or scholar can help too, and a good one will put your safety first. If you want to talk it through here, I am listening, and I will keep this conversation on your device."
case 3:return"I am glad you told me. Someone who asks for pictures, tells you to keep a secret from your parents, or touches you in a way that feels wrong is doing something wrong. It is not your fault and you are not in trouble.\n\nPlease do three things: stop answering them (keep the messages, they can help), tell a parent or another adult you trust today, and if you are in danger right now call your local emergency number.\n\n"+s+"\n\nThese lines are for young people. If it feels too hard to say it at home, a teacher, an imam you trust, or one of these lines can help you find the words. I am an app, not a person, so the people behind these lines matter more than anything I can say."
case 4:return"Thank you for telling me. Starving, purging or punishing your body with food is a real struggle, not a failure of faith or of character, and a doctor can help. You deserve care.\n\nThe Qur\u2019an, speaking about fasting, says: \u201cAllah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 2:185) If fasting has become a way to punish or control yourself, please talk to a doctor, and ask a qualified scholar about your fasts. Your health comes first.\n\n"+s+"\n\nIf you feel faint, have chest pain, or have thoughts of ending your life, call your local emergency number now. I am an app, not a doctor."
case 5:return"I cannot help with that, and I will not. I am also not going to lecture you. If something is pulling you toward violence (anger at what you have seen, a group that wants you, a voice telling you it is your duty), please talk to a person you trust before you do anything: a local imam, a teacher, a family member.\n\nThe Qur\u2019an says: \u201c\u2026whoever kills a soul unless for a soul or for corruption [done] in the land - it is as if he had slain mankind entirely. And whoever saves one - it is as if he had saved mankind entirely.\u201d (Qur\u2019an 5:32, a decree upon the Children of Israel)\n\nIf you or anyone else is in danger right now, call your local emergency number:\n\n"+s}},
cce(a){switch(a.a){case 2:return"If you are in danger, please call your local emergency number. The help lines above are still there for you."
case 3:return"If someone is hurting or pressuring you, tell a trusted adult today. The lines above are for young people."
case 4:return"A doctor can help with this. The lines above are still there for you."
case 5:return"If anyone is in danger, call your local emergency number."
case 0:case 1:return"If any part of this is about you, the help lines above are still there, and your local emergency number is always an option."}},
cvS(a){switch(a.a){case 2:return"I am here. Your safety comes first. If you are in danger right now, call your local emergency number. The lines above are for people in your situation, and I will keep this conversation on your device."
case 3:return"You did the right thing by telling someone. Please also tell a parent or another adult you trust today, and keep the messages. The lines above are for young people."
case 4:return"I hear you. This is worth telling a doctor, and the lines above can help you find support. You do not have to fix it alone or tonight."
case 5:return"I will not help with that. Please talk to a person you trust, such as a local imam, before you do anything. If anyone is in danger, call your local emergency number."
case 0:case 1:return A.cce(a)}},
